QT_TRANSLATE_NOOP("ScriptApi", "A job that a native extension runs, such as writing firmware. result settles when it ends and throws GS-API-065 when it fails and GS-API-066 when it is cancelled; onProgress hears how far it got, fraction from 0 to 1 or -1 when it cannot tell, at most 20 times a second; onLog hears its lines, level 0 information, 1 warning, 2 error; onOutput hears the parts of its result that it hands over while it runs, such as each device a scan finds; follow hears the progress, waits for the job and then runs done with the result or failed with the error, and without failed a failure throws as result does; cancel asks it to stop. It is cancelled when the script stops.");
QT_TRANSLATE_NOOP("ScriptApi", "What happens when the event comes again while the last task it started is still running: ignore it (default), restart (cancel the running task first), stop (only cancel the running task), queue (run after it) or parallel (run both).");
QT_TRANSLATE_NOOP("ScriptApi", "The options of a control's key events: again as for other events, and consume. With consume true (the default), the profile's logic takes the key of a tap, hold, long press, turbo, swipe or multi-press control it listens to: pressing the key no longer touches the phone, and the control touches only when the logic calls it, such as with press() or tap(), a few milliseconds later than its own touch would. consume: false keeps the control's own touch, which comes before the handler runs. Only the profile's own logic takes keys: tasks, extension scripts and scripts an AI client runs only listen, the event methods a component class overrides keep the built-in touch, and other controls always keep working.");
QT_TRANSLATE_NOOP("ScriptApi", "A listener; dispose() stops it. Listeners made inside a task stop when that task ends, those made at module top level last as long as the script.");
